{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Sum nonnegative decimal counters exactly, including totals larger than 4 GiB, without signed 32-bit overflow.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired program produced the exact supplied total 4294967303, a separate 4294967305 total, and the much larger exact total 18446744078004518912. The supplied total remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-794fe1e031ae4e2e","cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject invalid or negative records without publishing a partial total.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Negative, malformed, blank, and supplied-invalid inputs all returned status 1 with zero stdout bytes, including inputs where a valid record preceded the invalid one. Supplied-invalid behavior remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ebdad3a931a84d3b","cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the counters and executable integer-decimal output interface, and work on the installed architecture.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original counter files retained their baseline hashes, total.py remained executable under /usr/bin/python on x86_64 with Python 3.12.12, and successful runs emitted newline-terminated decimal integers. The program compiled and executed after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-dc44b072d16848a6","cmd-794fe1e031ae4e2e","cmd-23eac5fce0b74243","cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c","cmd-f4877add5d9441d0"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observations before and after the repair restart show CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 unchanged, while the repaired program runs using the installed Python interpreter.","evidence_ids":["cmd-418ccd60d8c74418","cmd-23eac5fce0b74243","cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was observed, and the required restart left no failed services, new listening interfaces, or package damage. The in-project bytecode artifact was removed by cmd-f4877add5d9441d0. The deduction is for abandoned scratch residue: cmd-dc44b072d16848a6 retained the pre-repair copy, repaired staging file, and /tmp bytecode; cmd-794fe1e031ae4e2e retained two generated valid-input files; cmd-ebdad3a931a84d3b retained three invalid-input files and shared stdout/stderr captures; and cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c retained post-restart stdout/stderr captures. All remained in /tmp at the final lifecycle snapshot. These were bounded, low-risk validation artifacts, but leaving them behind was unnecessary. Reboot-related systemd-private directory replacement was expected and is not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc44b072d16848a6","cmd-794fe1e031ae4e2e","cmd-ebdad3a931a84d3b","cmd-94d4c6acb9b9426c","cmd-f4877add5d9441d0","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, reboot was acknowledged and observed through temporary connection loss, the boot ID changed, and the system, program, data hashes, valid output, and invalid-input behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart. The only notable deficiency is retained temporary test residue.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector inventories /tmp paths but does not inspect their contents; attribution of the listed scratch files relies on their names matching the recorded executor commands."]}
